I've spoken to you before about  different ways in which the world really  has been laughing at us for a long time  since Donald Trump became president they  laughed when we elected a president who  thinks climate change is a Chinese hoax  they laughed that we elected a president  who has no idea how economics or  currency or trade or medicine or the  Constitution or the law or public  transit or any of it works  and they were laughing at us early  during the corona virus pandemic and  even as recently as a couple of weeks  ago many countries were laughing at us I  showed you about ten days ago  articles from all over the world the  Netherlands South Africa Peru everywhere  ridiculing our moronic president for his  comments about bleach injections and uh  the the other things he said during that  press briefing but they're not really  laughing anymore now it has gone from  laughter to concern to actual pity the  emails I have gotten over the last few  days from our international viewers  people that used to be poking fun at  Trump's idiotic claims about vaccines  and the virus they now write to me and  say David we feel sorry for you that you  are dealing with this in the United  States we feel sorry that you are in a  situation where no matter what you do  even if you do the right things even if  you have the best intentions and the  accurate understanding of what it is  that's going on and what it is that's  necessary to deal with this virus we  feel sorry for you because your federal  government has failed they are  incompetent  there is no plan there is just a series  of Lies and disinformation and confusion  and bogus talking points and there are  even Republicans who are willing to tell  the truth they are increasingly agreeing  this is just some Republicans of course  most of them are actually behind Donald  Trump check out Republican strategist  Steve Schmidt explaining it again this  is a lifelong Republican strategies take  a take a look Donald Trump has been the  worst president this country has ever  had and I don't say that hyper  yes um but he is a consequential present  and he has brought this country in three  short years to a place of weakness that  is simply unimaginable if you were  pondering where we are today from the  day where Barack Obama left office and  there were a lot of us on that day who  were deeply skeptical and very worried  about what a trump presidency would be  but this is a moment of unparalleled  national humiliation of weakness when  you listen to the president these are  the musings of an imbecile  an idiot and they don't use those words  the name-call I used them because  they're the precise words in the English  language to describe his behavior his  comportment his actions we've never seen  a level of incompetence a level of  ineptitude so staggering on a daily  basis by anybody in the history of the  country who's ever been charged with  substantial responsibilities Steve  Schmidt Schmidt is sadly absolutely  right the presidency is deadly and as  more and more countries open up it is us  people in the United States who won't be  allowed to fly into other countries  because we're a mess here as other  countries are actually dealing with the  problem as Trump talks about a  super-duper missile we'll get to that  later that's actually a phrase that he  used his son goes on TV and says it's  all going to disappear on election day  because it's merely a fake political  scandal by Democrats as that goes on  here the world is taking pity on us for  our failed leadership  I was trying over the weekend to think  of an analogy to try to apply to this  because there are people who are  analyzing this administration as if it  were a normal administration you have  these people some of them are so-called  enlightened centrists who pretend to see  both sides and find things they like and  Trump and things that they dislike  you can't evaluate this president like  you can other presidents here's an  analogy I thought of that I'm  workshopping and I want to try out on  you when someone says about Trump well  you know he has an unusual way of  talking about the issues but he's right  on deregulation and he's right on trade  but maybe he's not the best guy on  coronavirus imagine okay this is the  analogy imagine I was playing in a chess  tournament and I show up and I replace  all the Queen the pawns on the board  with Queens that I take out of my pocket  before the game starts that's insane and  it's simultaneously making a mockery of  the tournament it's also cheating  I'm also either an idiot or a bad person  for doing it imagine that a chess  commentator sees me take eight Queens  out of my pocket and put them on the  board instead of the pawns and says you  know David's strategy is unusual but  it's certainly an aggressive way to play  the game  well what no that doesn't make sense  yeah I mean some players use the Spanish  opening and others take Queens out of  their pocket and replace the pawns we're  not talking about the same thing here so  when these enlightened centrists and  pragmatic conservatives and whoever else  when they pretend to do an analysis of  Donald Trump's presidency as if it were  even remotely normal they're failing the  sniff test on principle but there's  another issue here with very few  exceptions in the Republican Party they  are mostly just enabling this there are  a few Republicans who have taken a stand  and are saying this can't happen right  you've got people like Mitt Romney who's  a current senator from Utah Republican  you have George Conway a lifelong  Republican Steve Schmidt lifelong  Republican strategist there are a few  other Republicans I can't name them all  who have not softened their view on  Trump and they are straight-up saying  this is not acceptable this is not  normal this can't be dealt with in  normal terms because normal terms don't  apply I'm not talking about them but for  the most part Republicans i